            <ArticleTitle>Antiphospholipid syndrome leading to myocardial infarction in a Fontan patient 17 years after Norwood palliation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1747-0803.2008.00217.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Appropriate regimens for anticoagulation in the single ventricle population remain controversial and are usually based on individual practitioners' preferences. We present the case of a patient with a history of hypoplastic left heart syndrome and Norwood palliation who presented at 17 years of age with an acute myocardial infarction and a new diagnosis of antiphospholipid syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
